q("wc-111", I, 1, WC, "Why can people not drink sea water straight from the sea?", "It has too much salt in it", [W("It has no water in it", "wrong-idea", "Sea water is mostly water."), W("It has too little salt in it", "reversed", "The salt is the problem."), W("It is too warm to drink", "wrong-idea", "Temperature is not the problem.")], ["The salt in sea water makes it unfit to drink."], None)
q("wc-112", I, 1, WC, "Why do countries store rain water in reservoirs?", "To keep fresh water for later use", [W("To stop clouds from forming", "wrong-idea", "Storing rain does not affect clouds."), W("To make the sea salty", "wrong-idea", "Reservoirs have nothing to do with sea salt."), W("To keep the water from evaporating at all", "wrong-idea", "Some water still evaporates from reservoirs.")], ["A reservoir gives a store of fresh water."], None)
