q("wc-117", I, 2, WC, "A celery stalk is placed in red water for one day. Red lines are seen inside the stalk. What does this show?", "Water moves up through the stalk", [W("Water moves down from the leaves", "reversed", "The red colour shows the water going up from the cut end."), W("The stalk makes red water", "wrong-idea", "The colour came from outside."), W("The stalk gives out water from its cut end", "wrong-idea", "The water entered the stalk.")], ["Plants carry water up through tubes in the stem."], None)
q("wc-118", I, 2, WC, "On a very hot afternoon a plant wilts, but it stands up again after being watered. Why did it wilt?", "It lost water faster than the roots took it in", [W("Its roots took in far too much water", "reversed", "Too much water does not make a plant wilt."), W("Its leaves made far too much food to hold", "wrong-idea", "Making food does not make a plant droop."), W("Its stem grew too long to stand up", "wrong-idea", "Stem length does not change in one afternoon.")], ["A plant wilts when it loses more water than it takes in."], None)
q("wc-119", I, 2, WC, "On a hot day we sweat a lot. How does sweating help the body?", "Sweat takes heat away as it dries", [W("Sweat adds heat to the skin", "reversed", "Evaporating sweat takes heat away."), W("Sweat makes the skin thicker and tougher", "wrong-idea", "Sweat does not change the thickness of skin."), W("Sweat stops the blood from moving", "wrong-idea", "Blood keeps moving.")], ["Sweat evaporates and takes heat away, so the body cools."], None)
q("wc-120", I, 2, WC, "Which job does water do inside the human body?", "It forms most of the blood that carries food", [W("It makes the bones hard and strong", "wrong-idea", "Bones are hardened by other materials, not water."), W("It makes the air that the lungs breathe", "wrong-idea", "Water does not make air."), W("It stops us from ever feeling thirsty", "wrong-idea", "Drinking water does this, but it is not a job of water in the body.")], ["Blood is mostly water and carries food and oxygen."], None)
q("wc-121", I, 3, WC, "Which two actions both help to save water?", "Washing a car with a bucket and watering plants with rinse water", [W("Washing a car with a hose and leaving the tap on", "wasting", "Both waste water."), W("Washing a car with a bucket and leaving a tap dripping", "mixed", "A dripping tap wastes water."), W("Watering plants with rinse water and using a hose to wash the path", "mixed", "A hose wastes water.")], ["A bucket uses less water than a hose. Rinse water is reused."], None)
